From 02be7a6dd317eebe55c172d72ce6ad5c9da6dc1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 6 <phase6@openwch.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 18:40:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] c-family: add the WCH 'highcode-gen-section-name'
 parameter

WCH's 8.2.0 carries exactly one private --param.  Two behaviours hang off
the exact, case-sensitive .highcode section name: the declaration is kept
out of line whatever the parameter says, and with the parameter set to 1 it
additionally gets a section of its own, .highcode.<declaration name>, so a
linker script can place each one individually.

Placement.  The .highcode literal is present in the official cc1 and cc1plus
and absent from lto1, while the parameter name is present in all three
(tmp/toolchain_8.2.0/evidence/s1/optsweep/optsweep.md section 5, rows D4 to
D6; re-checked with strings over
ref/gcc/darwin-arm64/8.2.0/libexec/gcc/riscv-none-embed/8.2.0/, counts 1/1/0
for .highcode and 1/1/1 for the parameter name).  lto1 links varasm.c, the
RISC-V backend and params.def but not the C/C++-only c-family objects, so the
section rewrite can only live in c-family; the parameter is in lto1 too, so
it belongs in the generic params.def rather than beside a target.  Hence
gcc/c-family/c-attribs.c and gcc/params.def.

Spec source, all first-hand measurements of the official binary
ref/gcc/darwin-arm64/8.2.0/bin/riscv-none-embed-gcc.

Archived cases, tmp/toolchain_8.2.0/evidence/s1/probes/raw: 06-hidden-options
gives the option surface -- help-gcc-params.stdout line 210 is the name with
default 0, minimum 0, maximum 1; param-highcode-bare and param-bogus give the
malformed-argument and unknown-name diagnostics, which the DEFPARAM
mechanism reproduces unchanged.  07-c-attributes gives the section
behaviour: hc-def and hc-p0 are byte-identical, so the default and an
explicit zero agree, while hc-p1 rewrites .highcode to .highcode.hf and
leaves .highcode.sub, .mysec and .mysec.sub alone.

Directed cases, tmp/toolchain_8.2.0/evidence/s3/d4/spec-probe/official.  q01
and q07 show an exact .highcode function is not inlined at -O2 or -Os -- the
unpatched compiler inlines the same static callee outright -- and q02 shows
always_inline over it is rejected as not inlinable, so the out-of-line rule
is unconditional and does not depend on the parameter.  q03 renames objects
too, function-local statics included, by their source names.  q04 shows the
suffix is the source declaration name, not the __asm__ name.  q05 shows
.highcode.extra, .highcode_init, .Highcode, ".highcode " and "highcode" are
all left alone, so the match is an exact strcmp.

Second matrix, tmp/toolchain_8.2.0/evidence/s3/d4/spec-probe/extra-official,
r1 to r3: a section attribute repeated on one declaration is rewritten once
and reports no conflict.  That is why the effective name is computed before
the previous-declaration check rather than only at set_decl_section_name --
comparing the stored, already-rewritten name against the raw attribute
string would make the second attribute conflict with the first.

The parameter help string is reproduced from the official binary verbatim,
including its missing capital and full stop.

9 new tests in gcc.target/riscv: 37 new PASS tuples.  gcc.dg/params/params.exp
and gcc.dg/dg.exp cover the two touched generic files and had no baseline, so
both were run on the host/0002 commit first; the parameter suite gains exactly
the two tuples params.exp derives from a new minimum and maximum.
